{title: 525 - Hiding in Thee}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #525 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 525}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]O safe [Ab]to [Eb]the Rock [Bb]that [Eb]is [Bb]high[Bb7]er than [Eb]I,
My [Ab]soul [Eb]in [Ab]its [Eb]conflicts and [Bb7]sor[Eb]rows [F7]would [Bb]fly;
[Bb7]So[Eb]sin[Ab]ful, [Eb]so wea[Bb]ry, [Eb]Thine, [Bb7]Thine, would I [Eb]be;
Thou [Ab]blest “[Eb]Rock [Ab]of [Eb]Ages,” [Cm]I’m [Eb]hid[Gm]ing [Bb7]in[Eb]Thee.
[Bb]Hiding in [Bb7]Thee, [Eb]hiding [Fm7]in[Eb]Thee,
Thou blest “[Bb]Rock of [Eb]Ages,”
[Cm]I’m [Eb]hid[Gm]ing [Bb7]in[Eb]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Eb][Ab]Hiding [Eb]in [Bb]Thee, [Eb][Bb]hiding [Bb7]in [Eb]Thee,
[Ab][Eb]Thou [Ab][Eb]blest [Bb7]"Rock [Eb][F7]of [Bb]Ages,"
[Bb7][Eb]I'm [Ab][Eb]hiding [Bb][Eb]in [Bb7][Eb]Thee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]In [Ab]the [Eb]calm [Bb]of the [Eb]noontide, [Bb]in [Bb7]sorrow's [Eb]lone hour,
[Ab]In [Eb]times [Ab]when [Eb]temptation [Bb7]casts [Eb]over [F7]me [Bb]its power;
[Bb7]In [Eb]the [Ab]tempests [Eb]of life, [Bb]on [Eb]its [Bb7]wide, [Eb]heaving sea,
[Ab]Thou [Eb]blest [Ab]"Rock [Eb]of [Cm]Ages," [Eb]I'm [Gm]hiding [Bb7]in [Eb]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]How [Ab]oft [Eb]in [Bb]the conflict, [Eb]when [Bb]pressed [Bb7]by [Eb]the foe,
[Ab]I [Eb]have [Ab]fled to [Eb]my [Bb7]refuge [Eb]and breathed [F7]out [Bb]my woe;
[Bb7]How [Eb]often, [Ab]when [Eb]trials [Bb]like [Eb]sea [Bb7]billows [Eb]roll,
[Ab]Have [Eb]I [Ab]hidden [Eb]in [Cm]Thee, O [Eb]Thou [Gm]Rock [Bb7]of [Eb]my soul.
{end_of_verse}
